    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="1162" n="1012" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1012"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1021/12–14.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Collier.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Adee informs Mr. Collier that the Spanish Chargé d’Affaires at Washington
                    paid to-day $28,500 interest and $570,000 principal in full of Spanish
                    inscriptions of 1834.</p>
            </div>
